# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the DishFlash React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1)
- **Files modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies (254 packages added)

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File modified**: `src/App.jsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the ThemeProvider wrapper at the root level
  - Placement ensures analytics tracks all routes and user interactions across the app

## Implementation Details

### Framework
- React 19.2.4 with Vite 8.0.1
- Following official Vercel documentation for React projects

### Integration Pattern
The Analytics component was placed at the root level inside the ThemeProvider, ensuring it:
- Has access to the theme context
- Tracks all routes managed by BrowserRouter
- Captures user interactions across all pages
- Remains active throughout the application lifecycle

### Verification
✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ No new linting errors introduced
✅ Dependencies installed and lock file updated
✅ Analytics component properly imported and integrated

## Next Steps
After deploying to Vercel, analytics will automatically begin tracking:
- Page views
- User interactions
- Performance metrics
- Custom events (if configured)

Visit the Vercel dashboard to view analytics data once deployed.

## Notes
- The integration follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide
- All existing code structure and functionality preserved
- No breaking changes introduced
- Compatible with the existing React Router setup
